      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: In or out
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - My thesis is due in a month.
    - If I put the river results in, my supervisor won't sign it off, the grant stops, and I probably have to start again somewhere else. A year, at least.
    - If I leave them out, I finish on time. And I give you the data, quietly, so somebody who isn't a student can use it.
    - A good scientist writes down what she sees. Nia taught me that. But I didn't think it would cost this much.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Publish the true results
      replyA:
      - In. All of it. Every sample.
      - If they won't sign it, I'll find somebody who will. Data is data. It doesn't care who paid for the microscope.
      flagsA:
      - bea_published
      - tower_file_soil
      optionB: Keep the grant, share the data
      replyB:
      - 'Out of the thesis, into your hands. Here: every sample, every number, on paper and on a stick.'
      - Keep it somewhere dry. Soil scientists are very fussy about dry.
      flagsB:
      - bea_grant_kept
      - tower_file_soil
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Quoted at city hall
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - My supervisor wouldn't sign it. So I took it to a professor at another university, and she signed it in five minutes and said 'about time someone did'.
    - And then Lucia Reyes read pages forty to fifty-two out loud at a city hall meeting. My pages! With my graphs!
    - No grant, no money, a year behind. I've never been this happy. Is that strange? Tariq says it's strange.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
